# Security response headers.
#
# ─── READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING THE SITE IS PROTECTED ───────────────────────
# This file is INERT on GitHub Pages. GitHub Pages cannot send custom response
# headers at all, so today none of the below is actually being served.
#
# It exists now so that migrating to Cloudflare Pages is a DNS change and
# nothing else — Cloudflare Pages reads this file automatically on deploy.
# Migration runbook: ~/.claude/plans/hi-i-want-to-immutable-charm.md §11
#
# The `.nojekyll` file in the repo root is what stops GitHub's Jekyll build
# from silently dropping this file for having a leading underscore.
#
# ─── KEEP IN SYNC ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Content-Security-Policy below must match the <meta http-equiv> tag in
# index.html, except for frame-ancestors — a meta CSP cannot express it.
# If you change one, change the other.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), usb=(), payment=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
